Bind-mount source for `docker compose`. Kept in git on purpose.

Docker creates a missing bind-mount source directory as root:root on the
host. The container then runs unprivileged, so the first write into a
directory Docker had to invent fails with EACCES — and for ./samples the
worse outcome is a root-owned directory appearing inside your own working
tree that you then need sudo to remove.

Shipping the directory means it always exists, owned by whoever cloned the
repository. Put samples you want to scan in here; everything except this
file is ignored.
